# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — react-router "RSC Mode CSRF Bypass".
# Not applicable: the web app is a client-side Vite SPA using BrowserRouter with
# classic <Routes>/<Route> (see apps/web/src/App.tsx). It does not use React
# Server Components / RSC mode, which is the sole attack surface for this
# advisory. The only fix is a major react-router 7 -> 8 upgrade, which we won't
# take on for a vulnerability we aren't exposed to. Revisit if we ever adopt RSC.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2

# --- Helm chart (charts/burnwise) config-scan false positives ---
# KSV0125 — "image from an untrusted registry": ghcr.io is Burnwise's own
# official image registry, so this is expected, not a risk.
AVD-KSV-0125
# KSV01010 — "ConfigMap stores sensitive contents": flags the key NAMES PORT and
# RATE_LIMIT_* as if secret; they are non-sensitive server config, correctly kept
# out of the Secret. False positive.
AVD-KSV-01010
